  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.3. Increased capacity of Member States to develop gender-responsive legislation, policies and measures for a world of work free from violence and harassment</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">To ensure the application in practice of Convention No. 190, significant changes and supplements were made to the Labour Code of the Republic of Armenia in May 2023 with an effective date of 1st, August 2023. In particular, a new article (Article 3.3) on violence and harassment was added to the amended Labour Code. Those amendments were initiated by the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs (MoLSA) based on the Republic of Armenia 2021-2026 Programme, which sets an objective of simplifying and improving the mechanisms for regulation of labour relations by bringing them into compliance also with the requirements of the international commitments. 

Following to the amendments to the Labour Code, the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs of the Republic of Armenia has expressed interest in initiating ratification of C190 and a gap analysis has been initiated. The ILO supported the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs by providing technical guidance through reviewing the proposed amendments of the Labour Code from ILS perspective and preparing a new formulation of the Article No. 3.3 during the amendment of the Labour Code. In response to the official request of the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, the ILO delivered a Gaps Analysis of C190 as a first preparatory step of ratification process of the Convention, to be validated by the tripartite constituents.</narrative>
   </description>
